zink: build on SiliconForest without MoltenVK (EXPERIMENTAL, not applied by any recipe)

On Darwin zink assumes macOS + MoltenVK (Objective-C mode, MoltenVK headers, no dma-bufs,
"@rpath/libvulkan.1.dylib"). SiliconForest is a DRM system with a native Vulkan driver behind the
Khronos loader: with -Dmoltenvk-dir unset, ZINK_NO_MOLTENVK keeps zink on its Linux paths and
dlopens libvulkan.1.dylib by leaf name. Builds (gallium-drivers=asahi,softpipe,zink, dev tree,
14 November). On the M1 it does NOT work yet: EGL's DRM screen with MESA_LOADER_DRIVER_OVERRIDE=zink
fails ("DRI2: failed to load driver") and EGL falls back to surfaceless swrast; the reason inside
zink was not established (SF-AC).

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/meson.build
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/meson.build
@@ -55,10 +55,16 @@
 )
 
 zink_c_args = []
+zink_cpp_args = []
 inc_zink_vk = []
 zink_link_args = []
 
-if host_machine.system() == 'darwin'
+if host_machine.system() == 'darwin' and with_moltenvk_dir == ''
+  # SiliconForest: a DRM system with a native Vulkan driver (Honeykrisp) behind the Khronos loader;
+  # no MoltenVK, no Objective-C, dma-bufs as on Linux.
+  zink_c_args += ['-DZINK_NO_MOLTENVK']
+  zink_cpp_args += ['-DZINK_NO_MOLTENVK']
+elif host_machine.system() == 'darwin'
 
   # MoltenVK options
   if with_moltenvk_dir != ''
@@ -106,6 +112,7 @@
     idep_vulkan_wsi_defines, idep_vulkan_util, dep_libdrm, vulkan_wsi_deps, idep_ntv,
   ],
   c_args: zink_c_args,
+  cpp_args: zink_cpp_args,
 )
 
 zink_deps = [libzink]
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c
@@ -70,7 +70,9 @@
